  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Core Tools**\n\nI\'m currently focused on structuring the foundational elements for `Canvas India`. My initial step involves clearly defining the tool types within `src/types.ts`. I\'m starting by enumerating the core tools like brush, pen, highlighter, and eraser, then extending this list to include more specialized tools like spray, calligraphy, mandala, shape, stamp, and text.\n\n\n**Expanding Shape Palette**\n\nI\'ve been adding more shape primitives, focusing on those relevant to Indian art. I\'ve included `circle`, `rect`, `triangle`, `star`, `lotus`, `paisley`, and `chakra`. I\'m also working on symmetry segments for mandala-like patterns, with options for `none`, `4`, `6`, `8`, `12`, and `16` segments.\n\n\n**Adding Cultural Context**\n\nI\'m now integrating more specific cultural elements. I\'ve expanded the shape palette with designs like Warli musician, Warli deer, and a Warli hut. I\'ve also incorporated Madhubani and folk motifs, including a royal peacock and the sacred fish, as well as festival symbols such as the Diya lamp, Kalash pot, Ashoka Chakra, and Dholak drum. I\'ve also added architectural elements like the India Gate and the Taj Mahal.\n\n\n**Implementing Interactive Feedback**\n\nI\'m now focusing on interactive feedback. I\'m building `/src/utils/audio.ts` for soft audio synthesis using the Web Audio API. This will provide subtle brush feedback and chimes for mandala completion and stamp placement. I\'m also preparing for the sound effect toggle.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 34195573
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
